1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,840
WTVA Action News at 6. I'm Drew Grant. Our lead story this evening, it's official. You

2
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:17,880
live in the best place in America. Every year, City Select Magazine lists the best places

3
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:23,560
to live in the United States. And this year, number one is right here in Charlottesville,

4
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:28,920
Virginia. Our reporter, Roberta Jackson, explains why.

5
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:33,480
When it comes to naming the best place to live in America, you might expect to see places

6
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:39,280
like New York City, Seattle, or San Francisco at the top of the list. But according to Kevin

7
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:45,520
Ingalls, editor of City Select Magazine, you need look no further than Charlottesville.

8
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:50,120
Among the advantages of living here, Ingalls says, are that Charlottesville has little

9
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:56,200
suburban sprawl and a beautiful natural environment in the foothills of the Blue Ridge Mountains.

10
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:01,640
Let's face it, who wouldn't want to live here during fall's amazing changing colors?

11
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:05,880
Or in winter with its perfect ski season, in spring when the flowers are blooming with

12
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:10,840
life, or even in summer when you can escape the humidity of the East Coast? And as the

13
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:16,680
home of the University of Virginia, Charlottesville has all the recreational and educational opportunities

14
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:21,000
you could want in a small town. I'm standing here with Kenny Flint, a college

15
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,080
student and Charlottesville resident. Kenny, how did you decide to come to Charlottesville?

16
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:33,440
I grew up in New York City, concrete everywhere, air, pollution, all that traffic, you know.

17
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:38,640
Here I'm in the countryside, I look out my window at mountains. I feel closer to nature

18
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,800
in Charlottesville than I ever did back in New York.

19
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:45,560
But there's nature in New York too. What about Central Park?

20
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:52,560
Yeah, that's a great park with the lake and fountains and the art museums. But it's so

21
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:58,680
planned, you know? There are busy roads on all sides, so it's like man-made nature, and

22
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:05,160
I live miles from Central Park. I had to drive or take the subway there. Nature here in Charlottesville

23
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:09,760
is all around, and it's really natural. It's wild.

24
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:14,160
But does the natural beauty of the environment ever distract you from your studies?

25
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:19,720
Well, I've got to tell you. Sometimes I'm sitting in class and I look out at the trees

26
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,400
and mountains and my mind drifts off.

27
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:27,080
When choosing its winner each year, City Select also looks at the cost of living and the cost

28
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:32,080
of buying houses. Charlottesville's house prices are quite high, but the cost of living

29
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:37,600
is low, so this is a very affordable city. Of course, now that the secret's out, everyone

30
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,040
is going to want to move to Charlottesville.

31
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:46,560
Reporting live from Charlottesville, I'm Roberta Jackson. Back to you in the studio, Drew.

32
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:52,920
Thank you, Roberta. This announcement by City Select is not all good news, though. The number

33
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:59,920
one city on the list a few years ago was Ann Arbor, Michigan. Ann Arbor, like Charlottesville,

34
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:05,760
is a college town with a high standard of living, good public schools, and lots of natural

35
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:09,080
beauty, so many people moved there.

36
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:14,940
The increase in population has caused some new problems. There are now more cars, which

37
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:20,780
means that there is more air pollution and more damage to the roads. Another problem

38
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:27,560
in Ann Arbor is sprawl. As the city has become busier, both new and old residents have moved

39
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:33,860
out, bringing pollution and traffic to suburbs and nearby villages. The increase in demand

40
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:37,920
for houses also pushed up the price of buying a home.

41
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:43,360
For more on this aspect of the story, we turn to a city planner here in Charlottesville,

42
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:48,280
Fiona Maxwell. Fiona, can we handle an increase in population?

43
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:55,920
Yes and no. We have enough space to expand without creating sprawl and without destroying

44
00:03:55,920 --> 00:04:03,560
parkland. However, house prices in Charlottesville are already high, and we're going to need

45
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:09,800
greater housing diversity if the city expands. This is an exciting opportunity, but it would

46
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:14,880
be a shame if the cost of living here becomes so high that many people can't afford to live

47
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:17,560
in the best place in America.

48
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:22,600
One more question, Fiona. Which city would you choose as the best in America?

49
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:28,880
Well, I live here too, so I would of course say Charlottesville. But I think the big cities

50
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:34,720
can be great places to live too. Atlanta, for example, is a very well planned city,

51
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:39,480
and it's very affordable. But I still wouldn't move there.

52
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:45,340
Thank you, Fiona. So it sounds like this announcement may turn out to be a double edged sword for

53
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:51,400
our town. I guess we'll find out. For more on this story, be sure to check our website

